From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lutvzn <106083845+lutvzn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:58:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] qualcommax: ipq50xx: add support for Xiaomi Redmi AX3000
 (RA81)

Hardware specification:
- SoC: Qualcomm IPQ5000 (IPQ5018 family, 2x Cortex-A53)
- RAM: 256 MiB
- Flash: GigaDevice GD5F1GQ5REYIG SPI-NAND, 128 MiB
- Ethernet: QCA8337 switch, 3x LAN + 1x WAN (1 GbE), connected to the
  SoC MAC1 (gmac1) through SGMII (QCA8337 MAC6)
- WiFi 2.4 GHz: IPQ5000 internal (board ID 0x24)
- WiFi 5 GHz: QCN6102 on PCIe1, user PD 2 (board ID 0x60)
- LEDs: system blue/yellow, internet blue/yellow
- Buttons: reset, mesh
- UART: 115200n8 (GPIO 28/29)

Flash layout: the vendor U-Boot ("bootmiwifi") boots the "kernel" UBI
volume of either "rootfs" or "rootfs_1" (36 MiB each) and passes
ubi.mtd=<slot>. Images are installed into the inactive slot and booted
for a trial; the new system arms flag_boot_success=0 in preinit and
confirms the slot at the end of boot, otherwise U-Boot rolls back to
the previous slot on the next boot. The slot selection logic was
verified by disassembling the RA81 U-Boot.

Notes:
- MAC addresses: WAN at 0:art+0x0, LAN at 0:art+0x6. The calibration
  data (0:art+0x1000 and 0:art+0x26800) already carries the WiFi MACs.
- The board data files are the RA81/CR880x M81 BDFs for board ID 0x24
  (IPQ5000) and 0x60 (QCN6102) in the template revision used with the
  WLAN.HK.2.7.0.1 firmware (as distributed by the hzyitc QSDK port),
  repacked for qmi-board-id=255 with variant "Xiaomi-Redmi-AX3000". The
  board ID 0x24 matches the one recorded in the unit's ART calibration
  data and the cnss2.bdf_integrated value passed by the stock U-Boot.
  The older RA81 stock 1.0.33 BDFs (WLAN.HK.2.5) make the 2.7 firmware
  assert in phyrf_bdf.c (ANTENNACHAIN_AXIS_Z).
- The U-Boot environment is 0x10000 bytes (CRC verified).
- TSENS is left disabled: it is not enabled by the boot firmware on the
  IPQ5000 and some zones report bogus critical temperatures.
- NSS: the board includes ipq5018-nss.dtsi with the 8 MiB nss_region the
  stock firmware reserves (256 MiB of RAM). Wi-Fi uses firmware memory
  mode 2 with the multi-PD reserved-memory layout of the Mi Router
  AX3000T v2, swiotlb=1 and coherent_pool=512K as on the other 256 MiB
  boards. The board needs the ath11k 256M and NSS LOW memory profiles.
- The board data files are in ipq-wifi/files until they are in
  qca-wireless.
